.TH TIME-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-19" "time-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
time-revamped \- local and world clocks in the tmux status bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B time-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B time-revamped
shows the local date and time, any number of world clocks, a countdown, a
stopwatch, a clock change warning and the working hours every configured
zone shares in the tmux status line. Each world clock is coloured by the
hour at that place. Every clock comes from the system date and the
timezone database, with no network call unless geoip is on.
.PP
The entry point
.B time-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, which binds the menu key in one tmux call
and replaces the placeholders #{time}, #{time_date}, #{time_clock},
#{time_zones}, #{time_local}, #{time_until}, #{time_elapsed}, #{time_epoch},
#{time_iso}, #{time_offset}, #{time_week}, #{time_doy}, #{time_dst} and
#{time_overlap} in status-left and status-right.
.PP
In the jobs render mode each placeholder runs
.B status
on every status redraw, which reads the clock once. In the options render
mode one background process renders every clock the status line uses, by default
once a minute, one second after the minute changes, and writes them in one tmux
call. Run with no command on a terminal, the tool offers a menu.
.PP
The clock change and overlap checks run date with \-d on GNU, uutils and
BusyBox and with \-r on BSD, detected once per process. Dates are printed
under the C locale.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the keys and replace the status placeholders now. In the options render mode it also starts the daemon.
.TP
.B list
Print every tmux command apply would send, one per line, and change nothing.
.TP
.B status
Print one placeholder: datetime, date, clock, zones, local, until, elapsed, epoch, iso, offset, week, doy, dst, overlap. The status line runs it. The placeholder #{time} prints datetime.
.TP
.B card
Read everything now and print one row per figure.
.TP
.B menu
Open the world clock menu on the current client. The menu key opens the same menu.
.TP
.B calendar
Open cal in a tmux popup that stays until a key is pressed. A tmux older than 3.2 says so.
.TP
.B copy
Copy the time to the tmux buffer and the system clipboard, as iso, the default, or as epoch, and say what was copied.
.TP
.B mark
Set the stopwatch mark that #{time_elapsed} counts from.
.TP
.B toggle-format
Switch @time_revamped_time_format between 24H and 12H.
.TP
.B daemon
Render and publish every placeholder the status line uses, by default once a minute, until another daemon takes over or the tmux server ends. apply starts it in the options render mode.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, the popup, the core tools, cal, the clipboard tool, curl, the zone database, the configured zones, the settings, the keys it found bound and gum.
A settings row names any setting whose value it does not know.
Exits 1 only when a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha,
.BR catppuccin\-latte,
.BR dracula,
.BR nord,
.BR gruvbox,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-timezones
or
.BR \-\-work\-start .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value ,
and outranks the environment and the tmux option. Given to
.BR apply ,
it rides on the keys and on every status call.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI TIME_REVAMPED_ SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR TIME_REVAMPED_TIMEZONES .
It outranks the tmux option.
.TP
.B TIME_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B TIME_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B TIME_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B TIME_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default. A key set to off binds nothing.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_menu_key
Prefix key of the world clock menu, or off. The default is M-t, left alone when someone else holds it.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_calendar_key
Prefix key of the calendar popup, or off. The default is off.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_copy_key
Prefix key that copies the ISO time, or off. The default is off.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_mark_key
Prefix key that sets the stopwatch mark, or off. The default is off.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_date_format
Format of the date: YMD, MD, DM, MDY, DMY, hide. The default is YMD.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_time_format
Format of every clock: 24H, 12H, hide. The default is 24H.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_timezones
World clock zones separated by commas or spaces. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_compact
1 prints short city labels: 0, 1. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_zone_labels
Labels matched to the zones by position. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_zone_separator
Text between the world clocks. The default is a space.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_weekend_override
0 keeps the time of day colour on weekends: 0, 1. The default is 1.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_local_label
Fixed label of the local clock. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_local_source
Where the local place name comes from: timezone, geoip. The default is timezone.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_geoip_endpoint
URL that answers with the city. The default is https://ipinfo.io/city.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_geoip_interval
Minutes between geoip requests. The default is 30.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_morning_color
Style of hours 05 to 12. The default is #[fg=yellow].
.TP
.B @time_revamped_day_color
Style of hours 12 to 14. The default is #[fg=green].
.TP
.B @time_revamped_afternoon_color
Style of hours 14 to 18. The default is #[fg=cyan].
.TP
.B @time_revamped_evening_color
Style of hours 18 to 22. The default is #[fg=magenta].
.TP
.B @time_revamped_night_color
Style of hours 22 to 05. The default is #[fg=blue].
.TP
.B @time_revamped_weekend_color
Style of Saturday and Sunday. The default is #[fg=brightblack].
.TP
.B @time_revamped_sunrise_icon
Glyph for hours 05 to 08. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_morning_icon
Glyph for hours 08 to 12. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_day_icon
Glyph for hours 12 to 14. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_afternoon_icon
Glyph for hours 14 to 18. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_sunset_icon
Glyph for hours 18 to 20. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_evening_icon
Glyph for hours 20 to 22. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_night_icon
Glyph for hours 22 to 05. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_weekend_icon
Glyph for Saturday and Sunday. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_icon_position
Where the glyph goes in an entry: middle, before. The default is middle.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_reset
Style written after each entry. The default is #[default].
.TP
.B @time_revamped_relative_day
1 adds a +1d or -1d badge: 0, 1. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_work_hours
1 dims a zone outside working hours: 0, 1. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_work_start
First working hour. The default is 9.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_work_end
Hour working time ends. The default is 17.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_dim_style
Style of a zone outside working hours, or none. The default is #[dim].
.TP
.B @time_revamped_primary
Zero-based index of the zone to highlight. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_primary_style
Style of the primary zone, or none. The default is #[bold].
.TP
.B @time_revamped_countdown_target
Target of the countdown, YYYY-MM-DD or YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_countdown_label
Text before the countdown. The default is none.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_countdown_done
Text once the target has passed. The default is now.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_dst_zone
Zone the clock change warning watches. The default is the local zone.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_dst_horizon
Days ahead the warning looks. The default is 14.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_dst_label
Text before the day count. The default is DST.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_overlap_label
Text before the overlap window. The default is overlap.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_overlap_none
Text when no hour is shared. The default is no overlap.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_render
Jobs or options: jobs, options. The default is jobs.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_interval
Seconds between publishes in render mode, or minute. The default is minute.
.SH STATE
The plugin keeps these tmux options itself.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_mark_epoch
The unix time of the last stopwatch mark.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_published
The placeholders the status line uses, recorded by apply.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_out_<name>
Each rendered value in the options render mode.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_ticker_pid
The process that owns the options render mode.
.TP
.B @time_revamped_geoip_city
The last city geoip gave, with _ts and _lock companions.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
time-revamped status zones
time-revamped card
time-revamped \-\-timezones "Asia/Tokyo, Europe/London" status zones
time-revamped list \-\-json
.fi
.SH FILES
Nothing is written outside tmux options.
.SH SEE ALSO
tmux(1), date(1), cal(1)
